<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>With beer in mind, Tony went to the kitchen and triggered a proximity event which played a video on the stasis closet\'92s door. It was Andrea.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I put myself up for random allocation,\'92 the video said, with Andrea\'92s image planting her fists on her hips and jutting her jaw out in defiance.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91So what?\'92 Tony said to the rotting bananas in a bowl by the jar of whey protein. Both were on top of the cooking hubs, which neither he nor Andrea ever used. \'91That\'92ll take forever, if it happens at all.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Andrea beamed out of the stasis closet and Tony\'92s heart chilled.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>A table of data appeared, covering Andrea\'92s torso. Tony was annoyed he could no longer see her breasts. The table scrolled and highlighted a row. There was her name, Andrea Novetine, allocated to James Marrin.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91He\'92s an Information Integrity Manager,\'92 she boasted from the stasis closet\'92s surface, and Tony felt flatter than her cold image. \'91I\'92m moving up, boy. A Cleaner? What was I thinking?\'92 She laughed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony decided on affirmative proactiveness, then wondered if 
